WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.399
A stick is 6 centimetres long. It is turned by 15 degrees. How long is it now? Let us

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:10.641
think carefully. Turning changes its direction, not its length. The answer is 6.

00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:11.293
Great work!

00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:16.840
Two 7-centimetre sticks point in different directions. How much longer is one than

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.927
the other? Let us think carefully. Equal-length sticks have a difference of zero. The

00:00:21.927 --> 00:00:23.743
answer is 0. Great work!

00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:29.708
You rotate a 8-centimetre paper strip so it points upwards. What length will a ruler

00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:34.461
show? Let us think carefully. A strip keeps its length after being rotated. The

00:00:34.461 --> 00:00:36.158
answer is 8. Great work!

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:43.399
A stick is 9 centimetres long. It is turned by 60 degrees. How long is it now? Let us

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:47.755
think carefully. Turning changes its direction, not its length. The answer is 9.

00:00:47.755 --> 00:00:48.425
Great work!
